@page "/progress"

<PageTitle>Progress</PageTitle>

<section class="page-header">
    <p class="dashboard-label">Summary</p>
    <h1>Progress</h1>
    <p>
        This section provides a simple progress dashboard for reviewing nutrition, workouts,
        goals, and overall user activity.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="dashboard-stats">
    <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-number">0</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Meals Logged</span>
    </div>

    <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-number">0</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Workouts Logged</span>
    </div>

    <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-number">0</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Goals Completed</span>
    </div>

    <div class="stat-card">
        <span class="stat-number">0%</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Overall Progress</span>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="progress-layout">
    <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Progress Summary</h3>
        <p>
            This area is prepared for future charts, weekly summaries, daily history,
            and progress reports after real user data is connected.
        </p>

        <div class="progress-row">
            <span>Nutrition Tracking</span>
            <div class="progress-bar-shell">
                <div class="progress-bar-fill demo-width-35"></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="progress-row">
            <span>Workout Tracking</span>
            <div class="progress-bar-shell">
                <div class="progress-bar-fill demo-width-50"></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="progress-row">
            <span>Goal Planning</span>
            <div class="progress-bar-shell">
                <div class="progress-bar-fill demo-width-65"></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Next Steps</h3>
        <p>
            The next improvement would be connecting this page to real data from meals,
            workouts, and goals so users can see live progress.
        </p>

        <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>Connect nutrition totals</li>
            <li>Connect workout count</li>
            <li>Connect completed goals</li>
            <li>Add weekly progress history</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>